FastAPI

Introduction

FastAPI is a modern and high-performance Python web framework used to build APIs. It is easy to learn and helps developers create APIs quickly and efficiently.

What is an API?

An API (Application Programming Interface) allows different applications to communicate and exchange data with each other.

Features of FastAPI

- High performance
- Easy to learn and use
- Automatic API documentation
- Data validation using Python type hints
- Support for asynchronous programming
- Integration with databases
- Suitable for building REST APIs

Installation

Install FastAPI using pip:

pip install "fastapi[standard]"

Getting Started

Create a Python file named "main.py" and write the following code:

from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/")
def home():
    return {"message": "Hello, FastAPI!"}

Running the Application

Run the application using the following command:

fastapi dev main.py

The application will be available at:

"http://127.0.0.1:8000"

API Documentation

FastAPI automatically generates interactive API documentation.

- Swagger UI: "/docs"
- ReDoc: "/redoc"

You can use these pages to explore and test your API.

HTTP Methods

Common HTTP methods used in FastAPI include:

- GET: Retrieve data.
- POST: Create new data.
- PUT: Update existing data.
- DELETE: Delete data.

Example API Endpoint

@app.get("/users")
def get_users():
    return {"users": ["Ali", "Sara", "Reza"]}

When you visit "/users", the API returns a JSON response containing a list of users.

Applications of FastAPI

FastAPI can be used for:

- Building REST APIs
- Developing backend services
- Connecting applications to databases
- Creating machine learning APIs
- Connecting frontend applications to Python backends

Useful Resources

- Official Documentation: https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/
- GitHub Repository: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi

Conclusion

FastAPI is a powerful Python framework for building modern APIs. Its simplicity, performance, and automatic documentation make it a useful tool for backend development.